# Let-generalization: polymorphic identity function used at multiple types
# The function id has type ∀a. a -> a
# It is used at Int (42) and String ("hello")
# Without let-generalization, this would fail type checking (but eval still succeeds since types are advisory)
# With let-generalization, this type-checks cleanly
[id: [fn [let x@a] x]
 int_result: [id 42]
 str_result: [id "hello"]]
=== out
Dict({"id": Function(x), "int_result": Int(42), "str_result": String("hello")})
